# Redeploy After Commit (Cloudflare + local API)

Koyeb is **retired**. Do **not** run `koyeb services redeploy` or any other Koyeb CLI.

## Stack

| Layer | Where it runs | How it updates |
|---|---|---|
| Web | Cloudflare Pages (`vettr`) | Push to `main` auto-builds. `VITE_API_URL` is the stable Worker: `https://vettr-api.metzgerbuildsthings.workers.dev/api` |
| API | This Mac (`com.vettr.api` → port `3001`) | Code is live once the LaunchAgent is running that tree. After backend commits, `launchctl kickstart -k gui/$(id -u)/com.vettr.api` |
| Public API URL | Worker `workers/vettr-api-proxy` | Proxies to the current Cloudflare quick tunnel. Tunnel LaunchAgent (`com.vettr.tunnel`) syncs `TUNNEL_ORIGIN` |
| Database | Local PostgreSQL on this Mac (`DATABASE_URL` in `backend/.env`) | Migrations run on API startup (`runMigrations`) |

## Web (Cloudflare Pages)

- **When:** Commit changes `web/` and is pushed to `main`.
- **Default:** Pages auto-deploys. No extra CLI unless auto-deploy is off.
- Do **not** bake a `trycloudflare.com` URL into Pages. Keep `VITE_API_URL` on the Worker proxy (`scripts/sync-pages-api-url.sh`).

## Backend (this Mac)

- **When:** Commit changes `backend/` or `backend/src/db/migrate.js`.
- Restart the API LaunchAgent so the tunnel serves the new code:
  ```bash
  launchctl kickstart -k gui/$(id -u)/com.vettr.api
  ```
- Confirm `curl -s http://localhost:3001/health` shows the new version. The tunnel (`com.vettr.tunnel`) stays up; do not kill it for a routine API restart.

## Workflow after commit

1. **Web-only:** Push to `main`. Cloudflare Pages builds. Note that in the reply.
2. **Backend / DB:** Push, then kickstart `com.vettr.api`. Do not call Koyeb.
3. **Both:** Push, kickstart the API, and note Pages will build from `main`.
